1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:05,013
SOMA is a free, open-source desktop app for designing 3D parts with AI.

2
00:00:05,013 --> 00:00:07,535
Its own agent, SOMA AI, is built right in.

3
00:00:07,535 --> 00:00:13,600
You describe what you need, SOMA AI writes the model as code, and SOMA builds it and shows it to you.

4
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:20,360
In this tutorial, we go from installing SOMA to a finished part, and then look at the tools that help you get it right.

5
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:26,017
Get SOMA from somacad.app.

6
00:00:26,017 --> 00:00:29,734
The download page picks the right package for your system:

7
00:00:29,734 --> 00:00:35,760
an installer or a portable ZIP for Windows, a disk image for macOS, and an AppImage for Linux.

8
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:43,320
Python, CadQuery and everything else SOMA needs comes included.

9
00:00:44,817 --> 00:00:46,831
The packages are not signed yet.

10
00:00:46,831 --> 00:00:50,230
On Windows, SmartScreen warns once on the first start:

11
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:52,307
click More info, then Run anyway.

12
00:00:52,307 --> 00:00:56,147
On macOS, open the app the first time with right-click, Open.

13
00:00:57,583 --> 00:00:59,276
And the agent comes with it:

14
00:00:59,276 --> 00:01:00,484
SOMA AI is built in.

15
00:01:00,484 --> 00:01:04,353
If you already use Claude Code or another agent, that works too.

16
00:01:05,303 --> 00:01:06,827
SOMA itself is free.

17
00:01:06,827 --> 00:01:09,494
For SOMA AI, you bring your own AI:

18
00:01:09,494 --> 00:01:12,313
a ChatGPT subscription or an API key.

19
00:01:15,417 --> 00:01:16,626
This is the start page.

20
00:01:16,626 --> 00:01:19,307
Your recent models are listed here, with a preview.

21
00:01:22,017 --> 00:01:22,745
New to SOMA?

22
00:01:22,745 --> 00:01:26,385
Start tutorial walks you through the window in twelve steps.

23
00:01:26,385 --> 00:01:28,387
Here we go straight to New model.

24
00:01:32,684 --> 00:01:34,254
In the middle is the 3D view.

25
00:01:34,254 --> 00:01:37,774
On the right is SOMA AI, your agent, and on the left the sidebar.

26
00:01:39,417 --> 00:01:42,528
Behind every model is code, but you never have to touch it.

27
00:01:42,528 --> 00:01:44,427
You just tell SOMA AI what you want.

28
00:01:46,651 --> 00:01:49,580
SOMA AI is the first tab of the agent area.

29
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:52,168
The first time, it asks for a sign-in:

30
00:01:52,168 --> 00:01:57,821
your ChatGPT subscription, or an API key from Anthropic, OpenAI, Google and others.

31
00:02:00,451 --> 00:02:03,393
Before the first message, a short note names the risks.

32
00:02:03,393 --> 00:02:07,941
SOMA AI works inside the model's folder, and asks before it does anything outside it.

33
00:02:09,684 --> 00:02:12,949
The model menu picks the AI model it thinks with.

34
00:02:12,949 --> 00:02:14,881
The search finds one quickly.

35
00:02:14,881 --> 00:02:16,214
We take GPT-6.1 Sol.

36
00:02:18,851 --> 00:02:20,829
Now just describe what you need.

37
00:02:20,829 --> 00:02:22,251
We ask for a bookshelf:

38
00:02:22,251 --> 00:02:30,164
80 centimeters wide, 180 tall and 30 deep, from 18 millimeter plywood, with open shelves at the top and two doors at the bottom.

39
00:02:35,018 --> 00:02:39,808
Before it starts, SOMA AI asks about the details it cannot guess, all at once.

40
00:02:39,808 --> 00:02:43,308
Click an answer or write your own, then send the answers.

41
00:02:44,258 --> 00:02:45,849
Then it gets to work.

42
00:02:45,849 --> 00:02:48,501
Every step shows up in plain words:

43
00:02:48,501 --> 00:02:53,124
it writes the model, builds it, and checks the result itself.

44
00:02:53,124 --> 00:02:56,458
This takes a few minutes, so we speed it up.

45
00:02:57,408 --> 00:02:58,872
And here is the bookshelf.

46
00:02:58,872 --> 00:03:02,418
Every board is a part of its own, listed in the structure tree.

47
00:03:03,774 --> 00:03:04,583
Now we save it.

48
00:03:04,583 --> 00:03:10,784
SOMA packs the model folder with its full history into a single .soma file, like a CAD file you can keep and share.

49
00:03:12,741 --> 00:03:15,424
To change something, you can simply show it.

50
00:03:15,424 --> 00:03:17,864
Open Mark up and draw right on the view:

51
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:20,791
outline the spot, add an arrow and a short note.

52
00:03:25,941 --> 00:03:29,632
Send to agent puts the sketch into the message for SOMA AI.

53
00:03:29,632 --> 00:03:31,509
Add one sentence, and send it.

54
00:03:36,608 --> 00:03:38,738
And there is the drawer, right where we drew it.

55
00:03:41,175 --> 00:03:44,699
Values the agent made adjustable show up in the Parameters tab:

56
00:03:44,699 --> 00:03:48,783
the outer size, the number of compartments, the board thickness and more.

57
00:03:49,733 --> 00:03:53,692
Drag a slider or type a value, and SOMA rebuilds the model.

58
00:03:53,692 --> 00:03:57,383
The agent is not involved, and the code stays as it is.

59
00:04:01,075 --> 00:04:03,365
Reset all brings back the agent's values.

60
00:04:05,408 --> 00:04:07,407
Animations work the same way:

61
00:04:07,407 --> 00:04:08,028
just ask.

62
00:04:08,028 --> 00:04:12,578
Here, the doors should swing open, and then the drawer slides out.

63
00:04:16,741 --> 00:04:19,591
It shows up in the Animation tab, together with its steps.

64
00:04:23,807 --> 00:04:26,152
Press play, and it runs right in the viewer.

65
00:04:26,152 --> 00:04:28,177
Make video renders it to a video file.

66
00:04:31,707 --> 00:04:34,049
SOMA AI keeps every conversation of a model.

67
00:04:34,049 --> 00:04:37,668
The clock at the top lists them, so you can pick one up again later.

68
00:04:41,107 --> 00:04:41,973
Will it hold?

69
00:04:41,973 --> 00:04:42,572
Just ask:

70
00:04:42,572 --> 00:04:44,837
how much weight can a shelf carry?

71
00:04:47,974 --> 00:04:52,713
SOMA AI sets up a load case and runs a strength analysis with the finite element method.

72
00:04:52,713 --> 00:04:55,944
CalculiX comes with SOMA, so this runs on your own computer.

73
00:04:56,894 --> 00:05:01,024
The result opens in the Analysis tab, where the safety factor and the stress are shown.

74
00:05:04,361 --> 00:05:06,811
A section cuts the model open, to look inside.

75
00:05:12,794 --> 00:05:15,299
The exploded view takes the assembly apart.

76
00:05:15,299 --> 00:05:18,444
SOMA works out in which direction each part comes off.

77
00:05:21,661 --> 00:05:24,831
For the workshop, ask SOMA AI for a technical drawing.

78
00:05:29,395 --> 00:05:32,836
The Drawings tab shows every sheet next to the model.

79
00:05:32,836 --> 00:05:36,407
Drag the column wider to read the views and dimensions.

80
00:05:36,407 --> 00:05:38,485
Export saves them as PDF or DXF.

81
00:05:41,595 --> 00:05:43,871
Skills are the agent's extra knowledge.

82
00:05:43,871 --> 00:05:48,365
For a second model, a phone stand for the 3D printer, we open the Skills tab.

83
00:05:49,728 --> 00:05:51,717
Each skill has three modes.

84
00:05:51,717 --> 00:05:52,011
Off:

85
00:05:52,011 --> 00:05:53,926
the agent does not see it.

86
00:05:53,926 --> 00:05:54,663
On demand:

87
00:05:54,663 --> 00:05:57,830
the agent reads it when the topic comes up.

88
00:05:57,830 --> 00:05:58,346
Always:

89
00:05:58,346 --> 00:06:01,218
the agent follows it with every change.

90
00:06:02,661 --> 00:06:07,031
We set 3D printing to Always for this model, and enter our material and printer.

91
00:06:12,295 --> 00:06:14,153
This time we start from a picture:

92
00:06:14,153 --> 00:06:15,956
a quick sketch with measurements.

93
00:06:15,956 --> 00:06:17,705
The clip adds it to the message.

94
00:06:21,862 --> 00:06:25,192
SOMA AI reads the sketch and follows the printing rules on its own.

95
00:06:26,142 --> 00:06:29,152
A stand that is easy to print, in the material we chose.

96
00:06:31,809 --> 00:06:33,099
Finally, export:

97
00:06:33,099 --> 00:06:38,339
3MF or STL for the slicer, STEP for other CAD programs, and more.

98
00:06:39,775 --> 00:06:44,078
If you want, you can use the AI agent you always use instead of SOMA AI.

99
00:06:44,078 --> 00:06:47,425
In this example, we use Claude Code to change the shelf.

100
00:06:52,275 --> 00:06:54,463
Open the plus menu and pick your agent.

101
00:06:54,463 --> 00:06:58,165
Here, Claude Code starts right next to SOMA AI, on the same model.

102
00:07:00,042 --> 00:07:02,412
We ask it for two round knobs on the doors.

103
00:07:04,962 --> 00:07:06,507
And there are the knobs.

104
00:07:06,507 --> 00:07:08,117
Same model, same history.

105
00:07:11,062 --> 00:07:11,816
That's SOMA.

106
00:07:11,816 --> 00:07:17,975
Download it for free from somacad.app, sign in to SOMA AI, and start with the part you need today.

107
00:07:17,975 --> 00:07:21,432
Press F1 in the app for the guide, or just ask SOMA AI.
